# **the output is the assertion.** `wrong has_value` on any line means the by-name lookup won and the
# guard called an overload the conformance never accepted - which is what this program used to print,
# followed by `-1` for a cell that was holding 42
--- OUT --->
42
9
-1
--- IR --->
# and the same thing at the symbol level, because the two overloads differ only in their receiver: `BCLC`
# is the const one `contract::unwrappable<V>` declares, `BMLC` the mutable one beside it. the mutable one
# is defined - it is an ordinary public member - and never called from a guard
CHECK: call i1 @_M4cell_has_valueZZMRBCLC4cell(ptr %__guard0
CHECK-NOT: call i1 @_M4cell_has_valueZZMRBMLC4cell(
